# Internationalization

Read `COPY.md` before editing copy. Supported locales: `lt` (default), `en`. Default LT URLs are unprefixed (`/…`); other locales use a prefix (`/en/…`).

## Where strings live

| Type | Location |
|------|----------|
| Shared chrome (nav, cart, footer, default SEO) | `messages/lt.json`, `messages/en.json` |
| Homepage | `messages/{locale}/home.json` |
| Original product page | `messages/{locale}/product-original.json` |
| Reviews page | `messages/{locale}/reviews-page.json` |
| Contact page | `messages/{locale}/contact.json` |
| Configurator | `messages/{locale}/configurator.json` |
| Checkout | `messages/{locale}/checkout.json` |
| Legal / long-form policy pages | `content/legal/{locale}/*.md` |

Page JSON is loaded **per route** via `src/i18n/load-messages.ts` (shared chrome + configurator always; home/PDP/etc. only on matching paths). When a section is reused across pages, register that dependency in `loadMessagesForPath` (pick keys when only part of a file is needed). Legal Markdown is imported only by `/privacy`, `/terms`, and `/warranty` — never through next-intl.

Prefer **page-level JSON files** when a page's UI copy would bloat the shared locale file. Prefer **`content/legal/` Markdown** for accordion-style policy pages. Keep shared chrome in the root `messages/{locale}.json`.

## Rules

- Never hardcode user-facing strings in components — use `getTranslations` (server) or `useTranslations` (client).
- When adding a string, add it to **both** locales with the same key structure. Do not rename keys.
- Do not change layout/data fields: `id`, `href`, `image`, `src`, `left`, `top`, `width`, `className`, `offset`, prices.
- Keep ICU placeholders (`{amount}`, `{count}`, `{name}`, …) identical across locales.
- Use `@/i18n/navigation` `Link` for internal routes so locale is preserved.
- After copy edits, run `bun run i18n:check`.

## Key structure

```json
{
  "cart": {
    "title": "Shopping cart",
    "checkout": "Checkout"
  }
}
```

## Language switcher

The navbar switcher uses locale-aware links to the same path in the alternate locale — do not implement locale switching via client-only state.
